## Tracks

> A **track** is a distinct workstream with its own objective. Projects grow by adding
> tracks, so this section exists from day one even when there is only one — and
> *"no further tracks yet"* is a valid, expected entry. Do not invent tracks to fill it.
>
> Tracks say what the project is trying to do. The work items within and across them
> live in `TODO.md`. Each track's slug (in parentheses) prefixes its item IDs there:
> `T-<SLUG>-<nn>`. Slugs are short, uppercase and permanent.

### Track 1 — [Name] ([SLUG])
- **Objective:** [The thing that has to work. This is the first concrete objective.]
- **Status:** [Not started / In progress / Done — one line; item detail lives in TODO.md]
- **Depends on:** Nothing — this is the first track.

**Further tracks:** [None yet.] Add each as `### Track N — [Name] ([SLUG])` with the same
three fields, and a matching section in `TODO.md`. When adding one, state explicitly
whether it **may depend on an existing track** or **must stand alone** — that constraint
is easy to state up front and expensive to retrofit once code exists.

